From c5cb0fa5e5eddceec99845b61e267e5fdd790883 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denis Mingulov <denis@mingulov.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Mar 2026 15:14:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: handle partial TCP reads and writes for large payloads

Server (TcpHostedService.cs):
  ReceiveAsync may return fewer bytes than requested because TCP
  delivers data in chunks. For large payloads (1MB+) this caused
  incomplete reads, leading to MessagePack deserialization failures.
  Replace bare ReceiveAsync with ReceiveExactAsync loop.
  Also fix TimeSpanToTimeout: .Milliseconds -> .TotalMilliseconds.

Client (tcpTransport.c):
  send() may return a short count on large payloads if the kernel
  send buffer is full or a signal interrupts. Add a send loop in
  sock_writerequest for both Windows and Linux variants.
  The recv() side already uses MSG_WAITALL.

Found by pkcs11-check (https://github.com/mingulov/pkcs11-check)
